    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73270.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "It is. I often said when I was in Congress for 16 years that I never would have been in the United States Congress had I not gone to Nassau Community College. It gave me the tools I needed at a an important time in my life. I still remember my political science professor, Professor Gerson, who kind of inspired me to think about Washington. I remember the extracurricular activities. And so it gave me everything I needed. It was just such an investment. I think community colleges around the country are undervalued. They are critical platforms for so many students in America. We need to be doing more for them and with them.",
