  {
    "episode_id": 73270,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73270.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. So I graduated in Nassau Community College, went to George Washington University, got my degree in political science, and I always dreamed, even growing up in Levittown in Wonton, Long Island, my dream was to one day be a member of the Congress. I started thinking about that all the way back and forth grade, the Gardeners Avenue Elementary School. So when I left Nassau Community, went to GW, still had that dream, worked on Capitol Hill as a staffer, and then decided the only way I'd ever be able to run for Congress representing Long Island was to get out of Washington and move back to Long Island.",
