  {
    "episode_id": 73270,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73270.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Yes. And so, around 2014, I began sensing that the anger in the american electorate building uh... and the tribalization on both sides of the aisle the uh... extremism uh... the fact that members of congress were just becoming uh... there were fewer and fewer members of congress to cooperate with everybody was just going into their corners and spewing and screaming and shrieking and i just i didn't get elected to congress to be part of that uh... and so i decided I didn't want to get trapped in that bubble. It was time for me to leave after 16 years. And so I came back to Long Island to pursue new curiosities. Throughout my life, I've been a voracious reader and my favorite places in the world are bookstores. When I was in Congress, Bill, my schedulers would always put on my schedule no matter where I was in the country or in the world, the location of the closest bookstore. I've been to Afghanistan and Iraq nearly 20 times. You haven't shopped at a bookstore until you've shopped at a book stall in Kabul where you can get mortar explosions in the distance. And when I left, I decided I just needed to purge myself of the venom and the sound bites and all of that Washington anger. And what's better way of doing that than to open my own bookstore where there are no soundbites. And sometimes it takes 300 pages of reading to truly understand something and not a sound bite on Fox or MSNBC. And I love it. So we opened three years ago. It is a struggle. It is a real struggle. Retail is tough, but we tell independent bookstores or even face even higher stiffer odds. But I love it every day.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Throughout my life, I have been a voracious reader.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "After 16 years in Congress, I decided to leave due to the toxic political climate.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Around 2014, I began sensing increasing anger in the American electorate.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "My favorite places in the world are bookstores.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "I did not run for Congress to become part of the divisive political culture.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
