    "turn_text": "And it seems it's a shame. People have said, you know, we got to get rid of Donald Trump. And I think that even if we get rid of Donald Trump, we have what I call bad yeast in the bread. So we have a bad loaf of bread. You can't extract just the bad yeast in that instance. But we need to do that as a country. The propaganda is incredible. And again, it goes back to what you say. People who haven't read books are not aware of these kind of, I guess, tools that people use to get their way in politics. It is scary. What's the experiment in democracy? It's 270-something years. Rome lasted five times as long and still fell. I wonder how long we have the things we all accepted before, like you hold the door for the guy behind you. When someone says good morning, you respond and say good morning. All of those normal things that most people",
