    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "but yeah it is looking politics you know you again as I said before you gotta you know if you run out of money you just raise more money if you're running out of public money you just extend the debt and print more money That's not a sustainable model or realistic model in owning a business. The other thing with the one similarity that I learned that I love is in politics, you have to appeal to voters. Well, in running a bookstore, you have to appeal to readers. And so this is an early mistake I made, to be honest. I thought, well, I know, you know, I love history and I love politics, so I'm just going to get all these books on history and politics and sell them. And then I realized, hello, I'm in a minority of people who love to read history, politics, people love, they want to read romance, they want to read Colleen Hoover, they want to read spy thrillers, they want to read self help, they want to read anything but politics and history. So I had to completely realign my inventory to reflect not what I was interested in. Not my positions, but the positions and interests and curiosities of readers. Very similar to a member of Congress who has to adjust in order to meet voters where they are, rather than where the member of Congress may think they are.",
