    "turn_text": "it's a balancing act. I went through it myself. I would say left of center. I was right of center on national security issues, right of center on muscular diplomacy, and right of center on deficits. I was left of center. on LGBTQ plus rights, left a center on protecting the environment, left a center on civil rights and civil liberties, which meant I was right in the middle, right? So which meant every time I cast, and so was my district, my district was defiantly moderate, which meant every time I cast a vote, I was pissing off 50%. If I cast a vote on the right, I was pissing off the left. If I was casting a vote on the left, I was pissing off the right. But that's what our founders envisioned, that you were going to take positions based on your own principles, but factoring in the consensus view of your constituents. And if they didn't like the way you voted, guess what? They get to fire you every two years. It's a perfect system.",
