  {
    "episode_id": 73270,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73270.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 68,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, the system seems flawed in that sense, is that I'm taking money from the people I'm supposed to, in the vein of corporations, in big business, I'm taking money from people who I'm supposed to be riding herd on, who I'm supposed to be watching. And there are so many things. Where did the consumer safety standards go? You read some of the fine print in these things and everybody's got to go to an arbitrator. You don't have a right to go to court if a product hurts you or kills you. It's the same thing we've talked about. We all have our cell phones. Did anybody read the terms and conditions when they got their cell phone? Everybody will tell you no. So then why do we let them keep writing them?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The system is flawed because it involves taking money from those one is meant to regulate.",
