        "text": "Regulators should not profit financially from the entities they supervise.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Consumers deserve the right to seek legal recourse in court for harm caused by products.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Arbitration processes are less fair or transparent than judicial trials.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Corporate influence undermines public safety and accountability mechanisms.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a moral obligation to protect consumers from exploitative contract practices.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "People would act more responsibly if they understood the implications of contractual terms.",
